        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="0858" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/9932</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4706</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received September
                        18</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    instruction No. 3676 of May 29 and to its cablegram No. 3750 of August 28,
                    relative to <pb facs="0859" n="573" xml:id="pg573"/> the pressing need for
                    knitting needles in the United States, I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    enclosed a copy of a note which has been received from the Foreign Office in
                    reply to my representations in this matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Irwin Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d761-a1.xml" xpointer="d761-a1"/>
            </div>
